cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite Rochette et al., Nature Biotechnology (2026),
  given below. A separate paper describing the bioinformatics and design tools in this
  package is in preparation; once it is published it should be cited alongside it.
title: "dgrec: analysis and design tools for DGRec targeted hypermutagenesis"
abstract: >-
  Python package for analysing DGRec (diversity-generating retroelement +
  recombineering) experiments and for designing template regions: genotype
  calling from amplicon sequencing with UMI deduplication, mutation-profile
  visualisation, RNA-folding-based scoring of TR sequences, synonymous recoding
  of poorly mutagenic TRs, and an LSTM model of TR-to-VR mutational profiles.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bikard
    given-names: David
    email: david.bikard@pasteur.fr
    affiliation: "Institut Pasteur, Université Paris Cité, Synthetic Biology Unit"
  - family-names: Régnier
    given-names: Léo
    affiliation: "Laboratoire de Physique de l'École Normale Supérieure, CNRS UMR 8023, PSL Research University"
  - family-names: Rochette
    given-names: Paul
    affiliation: "Institut Pasteur, Université Paris Cité, Synthetic Biology Unit"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/dbikard/dgrec"
url: "https://dbikard.github.io/dgrec"
keywords:
  - diversity-generating retroelement
  - directed evolution
  - targeted hypermutagenesis
  - recombineering
  - bioinformatics
# When the bioinformatics/design paper is published, add it here as a second entry
# (CFF "references:") rather than replacing this one - users should cite both.
